IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `ira-dates`
IMPORT `ira-rules`
IMPORT `ira-employee`

-- Industrial Relations Act 1979 (WA) -- worked cases for the employee's questions (ira-employee.l4) and the regulative
-- rule (ira-rules.l4). Every expected value was worked by hand from the deposited text; none was copied from the
-- encoding's output. Each assertion is a claim about the ENCODING on stated facts, not about the law. The facts are
-- illustrative; the prescribed amounts used ($185 000 and the like) are test figures, not the published indexed amount.
-- Weekdays worked from Thursday 1 January 2026.
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `cases`

`d` MEANS `the calendar date`

§§ `the regulative rule itself`

-- 28 days allowed: day 28 is on time, day 29 is not; a wait to day 29 with no step is a breach.
#ASSERT `the trace of` `the employee` `refer the unfair dismissal claim` `within` 28 `taken` TRUE `at` 28 `is fulfilled`
#ASSERT (NOT (`the trace of` `the employee` `refer the unfair dismissal claim` `within` 28 `taken` TRUE `at` 29 `is fulfilled`))
#ASSERT (NOT (`the trace of` `the employee` `refer the unfair dismissal claim` `within` 28 `taken` FALSE `at` 29 `is fulfilled`))
#ASSERT `the trace of` `the Commission` `start to deal with the application` `within` 14 `taken` TRUE `at` 0 `is fulfilled`

§§ `dates`

#ASSERT `is a leap year` 2028
#ASSERT (NOT (`is a leap year` 2100))
#ASSERT `is a leap year` 2000
#ASSERT `the last day of` 6 `years after` (`d` 10 3 2020) EQUALS `d` 10 3 2026
#ASSERT `the last day of` 6 `years after` (`d` 28 2 2024) EQUALS `d` 28 2 2030
#ASSERT `the last day of` 6 `years after` (`d` 31 12 2019) EQUALS `d` 31 12 2025

